# Nordlyse standards

These rules apply to every change in this project.

## Licences

- Third-party libraries, tools, and runtime dependencies must be MIT or Apache-2.0 only.
- Do not add GPL, proprietary, or other licences. If a needed library is not MIT or Apache-2.0, pick an MIT or Apache-2.0 alternative or ask.

## Git identity

- Push only as the nordlyse account (jakob.lyse).
- Author and committer: Jakob Lyse <jakob.lyse@gmail.com>.
- Never add Co-authored-by Cursor, cursoragent, or any other agent identity.
- On every push, check author, committer, and trailers before pushing. If another identity would appear, strip it first, then push as nordlyse.

## Language

- Comments, class names, README, docs, and commit messages are English.
- Chat replies may follow the user's language.

## Wording

- Do not use the word "create" in method names, class names, comments, README, docs, or commit messages.
- Use "add" or "insert" instead.
- Framework APIs that require that word may stay (for example document.createElement, Files.createDirectories).
